Gravitational-wave strain data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
js/data/gw/**
Derived from data released by the Gravitational Wave Open Science Center,
licensed CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  This research has made use of data or software obtained from the
  Gravitational Wave Open Science Center (gwosc.org), a service of the LIGO
  Scientific Collaboration, the Virgo Collaboration, and KAGRA.

Two datasets. gw150914.js holds decimated subsets of the published
band-passed figure strain. gwoscEvents.js holds 32-second excerpts of the
released 4096 Hz strain for five events, whitened, windowed, decimated and
quantized by this project, beside catalog values copied from GWTC-1 and
GWTC-2.1. Every processing step, the source URLs and their checksums are
recorded with the data, and `npm run gw:provenance` and
`npm run gwosc:provenance` regenerate them from the originals and compare byte
for byte.

Primary references: Abbott et al. (2016), Phys. Rev. Lett. 116, 061102,
doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.116.061102; the GWTC-1 and GWTC-2.1 data releases,
doi:10.7935/82H3-HH23 and doi:10.7935/qf3a-3z67; and the open-data papers,
Abbott et al. (2021), SoftwareX 13, 100658, and Abbott et al. (2023),
ApJS 267, 29.

